// **the one case that owns the shape of the entry point.** Every other IR golden in the corpus anchors on
// `define i32 @main(` and asserts nothing about its parameters, deliberately - so that widening it again
// is one edit here rather than fourteen.
//
// `stdlib: off` so that main's prologue is the *only* thing that touches the three globals. With the
// stdlib linked they are created by whichever of its bodies reaches a `process_*` builtin first, which
// makes their order in the module incidental - and a golden that depends on an incidental order is one
// that breaks for the wrong reason. Here the order is `gen_capture`'s own, which is the thing under test.
//
// nothing below reads any of them, which is the other half of the claim: the capture is unconditional.

echo 1;
